<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<wml>

  <card id="custlist">

    <!--
      Customer lookup — a subroutine of linebot.wml (a fragment, not a standalone entry point)

      Loaded by linebot.wml with <include name="custlist"/>. mywap.pas's
      _include copies this <card> over and runs it with ParseBlock, sharing the same
      Evaluator, so variables set here are visible in linebot.wml.

      [Why the file is not called cust.wml]
      WebHookAction uses the first word of the message as a file name and looks for <op>.wml. If this file were
      cust.wml, a user sending "cust" would load it directly as a full entry point —
      and since this file has no CDATA output section, the whole site layout would be sent to LINE.
      Giving it a name that cannot be taken as a command removes that path.

      [What this file does]
      It only sets reply_text and msg_json. quickReply and the outer JSON template
      are produced by linebot.wml; a subroutine should not produce its own, or there will be two sets.

      [Variables you can use directly] (already set by linebot.wml)
        user_text  — the full message the user sent (including the command word)
        cmd        — user_text in lower case, trimmed
        uid        — the sender's LINE userId
      plus the whole events_* series set by WebHookAction with SetVar.
    -->

    <!--
      Getting the keyword: find the first space; everything after it is the keyword.

      Why not $(p1): if the user sends only "cust", p1 is never created,
      and referring to it gives Unknown identifier instead of an empty string. Splitting it yourself has another benefit:
      the keyword of "cust north office" becomes "north office" (including the space),
      while p1 would only give "north".

      [Why the if condition also checks sp < LENGTH]
      Only MID can be used — the string functions registered in myexp.pas are just CHR/LENGTH/LOWER/UPPER/
      MID/POS/TRIM/INSTR, with no COPY and no LEFT (_COPY exists in the source
      but is not registered with AddFunctionParam, so calling it gives Unknown function identifier).
      And _MID is the DBCS version: when the start is past the end of the string, its internal j is never assigned,
      and it returns undefined content (_AnsiMid fixed this bug in V1.6; _MID did not).
      So we guard it ourselves: when the space is the last character, sp+1 is already out of range,
      which is the same as having no keyword.

      Note: a less-than sign in cnd must be written as &amp;lt;; XML attribute values do not accept a literal <.
    -->
    <setvar name="sp" value="INSTR(user_text, ' ')"/>
    <setvar name="kw" value="''"/>
    <if cnd="(sp > 0) and (sp &lt; LENGTH(user_text))">
      <setvar name="kw" value="TRIM(MID(user_text, sp + 1, 200))"/>
    </if>

    <!--
      kw is user input and goes straight into the SQL. Without filtering, a single quote could
      rewrite the query. AsSqlStr() doubles each single quote (the SQL literal escape);
      it does not add the outer quotes, so the SQL has to write '$kwsql' itself.
    -->
    <setvar name="kwsql" value="AsSqlStr(kw)"/>

    <!--
      ★ Table and column names: cu / cno / cname follow the naming convention of pa (the product table)
        and are an assumption; if your names differ, just change these three.

      [Why the whole list is built by SQL]
      <dbquery> only opens a dataset; it is not a loop — mywap.pas's _dbquery
      has no ParseBlock and no DataSet.Next, and its child nodes are field definitions (onevent
      and so on), not content run per record. After opening, $(id.field) returns "the current
      record", i.e. the first one.
      Walking records needs <report> or <crosstab>, but both are designed for producing tables,
      which is roundabout for building a piece of plain text.
      Instead MySQL joins the 10 rows into one string with group_concat; the result
      has a single row, so $(cu.txt) gets it directly, with no loop at all.

      [Why char(10) instead of separator '\n']
      The SQL string goes through the engine's preprocessing and $ variable substitution first, and it is not certain
      whether backslash escapes survive. char(10) is a plain function call and cannot be mangled.
      So each row appends char(10) itself, and the separator is an empty string.

      [limit 10]
      Not just for display: a single LINE message is limited to 5000 characters, and with many customers, sending them all
      at once is rejected with 400. Also, group_concat defaults to 1024 bytes
      (group_concat_max_len), plenty for 10 customer names; to raise it
      you have to change the MySQL settings.

      [When there is no data] count(*) returns 0 and group_concat returns NULL,
      so every value below goes through AsStringValue.
    -->
    <dbquery id="cu"><![CDATA[
      select count(*) as cnt,
             group_concat(concat(cname, '[', cno, ']', char(10))
                          order by cno separator '') as txt
      from (select cno, cname from cu
            where ('$kwsql' = '')
               or (cname like '%$kwsql%')
               or (cno like '%$kwsql%')
            order by cno
            limit 10) t
    ]]></dbquery>

    <setvar name="n" value="AsInt(cu.cnt)"/>
    <setvar name="lst" value="TRIM(AsStringValue(cu.txt))"/>

    <if cnd="n = 0">
      <if cnd="kw = ''">
        <setvar name="reply_text" value="'There are no customers in the customer table yet.'"/>
      <else/>
        <setvar name="reply_text" value="'No customers match: ' + kw + CHR(10) + CHR(10) + 'Send just cust to see the first 10.'"/>
      </if>
    <else/>
      <if cnd="kw = ''">
        <setvar name="reply_text" value="'Customers (first ' + AsStringValue(n) + ')' + CHR(10) + TRIM(lst) + CHR(10) + CHR(10) + 'To find a customer: cust keyword'"/>
      <else/>
        <setvar name="reply_text" value="'Search for &quot;' + kw + '&quot; found ' + AsStringValue(n) + CHR(10) + TRIM(lst)"/>
      </if>
    </if>

    <setvar name="msg_json" value="'&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:' + AsJson(reply_text)"/>

  </card>

</wml>
